  "description": "A parametric LED STRIP on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A SEGMENT and set Fit to host to Exact and it takes the full run. This is the object behind every concealed line in the bedroom plan: cove band, headboard halo, under the bedside tables, behind the TV and under the console — five uses, one body.\n\nTHROW IS THE SECTION, NOT A SETTING. Up sits the tape on the channel base and opens upward, Down hangs the channel and puts the tape at its ceiling, and Wash turns the whole section on its side so the opening faces along the wall. One flag each, and every later dimension is written in terms of them.\n\nRECESSED VERSUS SURFACE IS ONE LINE. `_rec` moves the channel's base plane relative to the mount elevation; nothing else in the body knows the difference.\n\nTHE CHANNEL IS A BASE AND TWO WALLS, not a filled bar, so it reads as an extrusion in section and the tape sits inside something.\n\nKELVIN AND OUTPUT ARE REPORTED, NOT DRAWN. They are real parameters carried to the Output Metrics node — `lumens = intensity × length` and a load at 90 lm/W — because a render needs them and geometry cannot express them.\n\nDIMENSIONS AT THE DEFAULTS: a 3.00 m run at 2.972 m, 24 × 15 mm recessed channel, 2700 K, 2700 lm, 30 W.\n\nWHAT THIS CANNOT DO. It is straight — a run around a corner is two strips. There is no emissive material and no light is cast; the renderer decides that. The diffuser is not modelled.",
